    <!-- Explicación de privacidad: un párrafo corto por <item>, en este orden. -->
    <string-array name="settings_privacy_paragraphs">
        <item>Reelometer counts what you watch on TikTok, Instagram and YouTube using Android\'s accessibility service. For each video, the app keeps the app, the time, how long you watched it, the creator and the description.</item>
        <item>Everything is stored on this phone. There are no accounts, no servers, no ads and no analytics. The app has no permission to use the internet.</item>
        <item>Your data leaves here only if you take it out yourself: when you export the CSV or share your receipt.</item>
        <item>If you turn off the service, it stops counting. If you delete the data or uninstall the app, it disappears.</item>
    </string-array>
